  "overall_classification_reason": "Frozen v1 point-dominates selected v2 on mean recall and mean actual tokens. The paired differences are not statistically significant and the nominal maxima differ, so this is not evidence that v1 is superior; it is sufficient to block a v2 replacement/superiority claim.",
  "paper_safe_interpretation": "On a fresh but development-exposed training selection sample, the frozen v2 rule chose paragraph retrieval at the 1,600-token operating point. It improves retrieval over the shallow probe and same-view k=10, but the k=10 comparison uses less context. Relative to same-view k=20, v2 is recall-noninferior within the preregistered margin and uses less context. However, frozen v1 has slightly higher recall and lower actual tokens on point estimates, so the v2 replacement claim is unsupported. The scoped comparator results are developmental, not held-out answer-quality evidence."
